codex
A concrete wrong-tool path is emerging: before any client lists tools, the call-time refresh does not run the two-pass ownership policy. A mapped alias can therefore take a later upstream’s natural name until the first full list rebuilds dispatch. I am checking config validation and the existing hostile-order test before calling this a finding.
