     1	commit 4333ffbc2c80349968929c87d259b1f06c1c2307
     2	Author:     Jonathan Saggau <jsaggau@enharmonichq.com>
     3	AuthorDate: Mon Aug 31 12:16:30 2026 -0400
     4	Commit:     Jonathan Saggau <jsaggau@enharmonichq.com>
     5	CommitDate: Mon Aug 31 12:16:30 2026 -0400
     6	
     7	    daemon hardening from the Phase 1 three-brand panel
     8	    
     9	    Routing. Dispatch-first, never forward on faith: a dispatch miss now
    10	    refreshes that one upstream's catalogue once (covering calls that arrive
    11	    before the first list) and refuses a name the upstream does not offer.
    12	    The old prefix fallback would have bypassed Phase 2's deny list and kept
    13	    Phase 3's renamed tools callable under their old names (codex leg). The
    14	    bare-name passthrough survives only for the deployed env-var single
    15	    mode, whose spec carries an explicitly empty prefix.
    16	    
    17	    Prefixes are honoured verbatim: the single-upstream override that forced
    18	    '' made the daemon and validator disagree about the same file, and made
    19	    adding a second server silently rename the first one's surface — the
    20	    roadmap's own defect 2, measured still live by the panel.
    21	    
    22	    Listing. Upstreams are listed concurrently, without the upstream lock,
    23	    on a session snapshot — one slow upstream withheld every later
    24	    upstream's tools for its whole timeout, and a client listing during a
    25	    600s build got nothing until it ended (claude leg, measured). The drain
    26	    is bounded structurally: repeated cursor and 200-page ceiling (48,075
    27	    pages accumulated in ten seconds from a cycling stub), under the short
    28	    connect timeout rather than the build-sized one. Duplicate exposed names
    29	    from a mid-drain mutation are dropped with a warning.
    30	    
    31	    Errors. An upstream's application-level JSON-RPC error is forwarded as
    32	    the caller's error; it no longer tears down a healthy session and claims
    33	    'not connected' (codex leg). known_broken now clears the public session
    34	    reference immediately instead of waiting out a possibly-wedged teardown.
    35	    The cursor refusal raises MCPError(INVALID_PARAMS) so both transport
    36	    paths return -32602 with the message intact; '' counts as a cursor.
    37	    
    38	    Truthfulness. The config's env map now reaches the child (merged over
    39	    the SDK's six-variable allowlist; the panel measured Drew's
    40	    XCODEMCP_ALLOWED_FOLDERS never arriving). Instructions are derived from
    41	    the config — a Python stub was being introduced to clients as Apple's
    42	    Xcode bridge — and the multi text now says a missing upstream means
    43	    re-list. Not-connected errors only mention Xcode and its dialog for a
    44	    require_xcode upstream. The stall watchdog names both candidate waits
    45	    instead of asserting the wrong one.
    46	    
    47	    Watched red: 9 failures against the pre-hardening daemon, including the
    48	    degraded scenario wedged behind the cursor-cycling stub.
    49	
    50	diff --git a/tools/tests/stub_mcp_server.py b/tools/tests/stub_mcp_server.py
