     6	
     7	    sieve/map hardening from the Phase 3 three-brand panel
     8	    
     9	    Composition is now two-pass: natural prefixed names reserve the surface
    10	    first, mapped aliases are admitted only where room remains. Ownership of
    11	    an exposed name can no longer depend on which upstream the config lists
    12	    first — the panel showed an earlier-listed alias hijacking a later
    13	    upstream's genuine name while the genuine tool silently vanished; the
    14	    suite now runs that exact scenario ('aaathief' claims alpha__ping by
    15	    alias and loses). A duplicated copy of an admitted mapped tool is
    16	    dropped instead of resurrecting its replaced original, and a doubly
    17	    colliding tool is warned off the surface by name.
    18	    
    19	    Descriptions rewrite from the EFFECTIVE table — old bare name to the
    20	    name actually published — so a degraded alias rewrites to its prefixed
    21	    fallback, never to a name not on the surface. Alternation is
    22	    longest-first (the panel measured 'use foo-bar' rewriting as
    23	    '<mapped>-bar' with config-ordered alternatives).
    24	    
    25	    The bare-name passthrough is gated to the env-var contract via a
    26	    from_env flag: a FILE config with an empty prefix goes through the
    27	    catalogued path, so its blocked tools are refused at call time instead
    28	    of being hidden-but-callable — all three brands found that bypass. A
    29	    single-server file config's dispatch misses route through the block
    30	    check and refresh instead of dead-ending on the prefix walk.
    31	    
    32	    The call-time refresh is add-only (setdefault): it can no longer
    33	    overwrite a name another upstream legitimately published, which was the
    34	    panel's worst finding — wrong-tool execution reachable from any dispatch
    35	    miss. Static config gains one more contradiction check: an exposed name
    36	    shadowing a blocked tool on the same server is rejected, because the
    37	    call path resolved that clash by timing. Standing warnings (collisions,
    38	    stale override descriptions) log once per key; stale-entry bookkeeping
    39	    forgives an entry whose tool reappears so a later re-staleness warns
    40	    again. The stale-alias call now names what was asked ('never_served',
    41	    not the prefix-stripped 'erved').
    42	    
    43	    Watched red: 7 daemon and 1 config failures against the pre-fix code,
    44	    including the live alpha__ping hijack.
